      'Removed AI-drafted milestones and metrics pending a settled direction.',
      'Removed AI-drafted publication and test-result claims from the site.',
      'Rebuilt the dev log with plain, fact-based bullet points.',
      'Set up a separate, private notes location for personal reflections.',
    ],
    personalNotes: `Add your own notes for this session here.`,
  },
  {
    date: '2026-09-14',
    title: 'Layout and styling fixes',
    aiSummary: [
      'Fixed a bug where the fixed header overlapped page content.',
      'Repositioned the hologram easter-egg element on the home page.',
      'Unified rounded-corner styling and button style across pages.',
      'Removed a placeholder diagram from the Project page.',
      'Removed an inaccurate personal-background detail from the About page.',
    ],
    personalNotes: `When revisiting the website on a different device, I noticed some of the padding and organization on the website was off - struggled for a bit to correct it`,
  },
  {
    date: '2026-09-11',
    title: 'Initial site build',
    aiSummary: [
      'Scaffolded an Astro + Tailwind site with GitHub Pages deploy.',
      'Built the page structure: Home, About, Project, Dev Log.',
      'Added personal photos and a short bio to the About page.',
      'Added a header, footer, and base layout shared across pages.',
      'Added an animated arc-reactor element and hover easter egg to the home page.',
      'Drafted an initial project one-pager and dev log template (later revised — see 2026-09-15).',
    ],
    personalNotes: `Jumped between models to explore cost and performance. Settled on Haiku and Sonnet as Opus was too expensive for the simplicity of the tasks performed. Used a combination of Claude Co-Work and Claude Code.  Used Co-Work to go through previously created files and come up with context that could be fed to Claude Code as it built the website.  I also used Co-Work to explore research directions and help scope something ambitious for this class. I had issues with misunderstanding context when using Haiku.  Switched over to Sonnet, and performance was better. Still have an error with the outlining of some text on the title page.`,
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout title="Dev Log">
  <section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 pt-12 pb-16">
    <h1 data-reveal="1">Dev Log</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-base text-space-200" data-reveal="2">
      A plain, fact-based record of what was built or changed each session,
      paired with my own notes on that same work. The left column is the
      objective summary; the right column is mine — written by me, not
      AI-generated.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-12 space-y-12">
      {entries.map((entry, i) => (
        <article
          class="relative border-l-2 border-orbit/30 pl-6"
          data-reveal={String(Math.min(i + 1, 5))}
        >
          <span class="absolute -left-[7px] top-1.5 w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-orbit shadow-orbit-sm"></span>
          <time class="font-mono text-xs text-space-400 tracking-widest">
            {entry.date}
          </time>
          <h3 class="mt-1 mb-4 text-orbit-light">{entry.title}</h3>

          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-0 rounded-xl border border-orbit/15 overflow-hidden">
            <div class="p-5 border-b md:border-b-0 md:border-r border-orbit/15 bg-space-900/30">
              <p class="font-mono text-xs text-orbit tracking-widest mb-3">SESSION SUMMARY</p>
              <ul class="text-base text-space-300 m-0 space-y-1 list-disc pl-5">
                {entry.aiSummary.map((bullet) => (
                  <li>{bullet}</li>
                ))}
              </ul>
              {entry.attachment && (
                <a
                  href={resolvePath(entry.attachment.href)}
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener"
                  class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 mt-4 text-sm text-orbit-light hover:text-orbit underline"
                >
                  ↓ {entry.attachment.label}
                </a>
              )}
            </div>
            <div class="p-5 bg-thruster-500/[0.04]">
              <p class="font-mono text-xs text-thruster-400 tracking-widest mb-3">MY NOTES</p>
              <p class="text-base text-space-300 m-0 whitespace-pre-line">
                {entry.personalNotes}
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          {entry.image && (
            <figure class="mt-5 rounded-xl border border-orbit/15 overflow-hidden bg-space-900/30">
              <img
                src={resolvePath(entry.image.src)}
                alt={entry.image.alt}
                class="w-full h-auto block"
              />
              {entry.image.caption && (
                <figcaption class="text-xs text-space-400 italic px-5 py-3 m-0">
                  {entry.image.caption}
                </figcaption>
              )}
            </figure>
          )}

          {entry.essay === 'debate' && (
            <details class="mt-5 rounded-xl border border-orbit/15 bg-space-900/30 overflow-hidden">
              <summary class="cursor-pointer px-5 py-4 font-mono text-xs text-orbit tracking-widest list-none">
                FULL ESSAY: TO ACCELERATE OR TO RESTRAIN?
              </summary>
              <div class="px-5 pb-6 pt-1 border-t border-orbit/15 essay-body">
                <DebateEssay />
              </div>
            </details>
          )}
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>

    <p class="mt-12 text-sm text-space-400 border-t border-orbit/10 pt-6">
      AI session summaries are on the left, and personal reflections are on the right.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style is:global>
  /* Long-form essay rendered inside a dev log entry. */
  .essay-body h1 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .essay-body h2 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--color-orbit-light);
  }

  .essay-body p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .essay-body em {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
</style>
